<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40681" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-curvus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>turned back</i>, <i>bent</i>, <i>crooked</i>, or <i>curved back</i> (a
				<b>poet.</b> word of the Aug. per.; also in
			post-Aug. prose; syn.: reduncus, repandus): cornu, * <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 7,
				513</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 5, 327</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. F. 5,
				119</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">puppis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. M.
					8, 141</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">11, 464</span></i>; <i><span class="en">15, 698</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fibrae radicis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 14, 632</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hederae nexus,</span>”
				<i>winding</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 3, 664</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tectum,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the Labyrinth</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. H.
					10, 71</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aera,</span>”
				i. e. <i>hooks</i>, <i>fishhooks</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. F.
					6, 240</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tergum (delphini),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 2, 113</span></i>
			 et saep.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conchae ad buccinum recurvae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 33, 52, § 103</span></i>
			.</div>
